job_description:
**About FACEIT**
As one of the core pillars of EFG, FACEIT is the beating heart of competitive online gaming. With over 34 million registered users playing 30 million matches each month, we are the industry leader in competitive play. Our platform is where gamers of all levels come together to test their skills, climb the ranks, and forge communities.
At FACEIT, we're relentless in our pursuit of excellence. We push the limits of technology, deliver cutting-edge features, and provide an unparalleled competitive gaming experience. Our vision is simple: to empower every player to reach their full potential, while keeping competition fair, engaging, and thrilling.
**The Problem You Will Solve**
Every month, millions of players decide whether FACEIT is worth paying for - and your code is where that decision happens.
Subscriptions is the primary revenue engine behind the FACEIT platform. It's a Stripe- and Xsolla-powered checkout, a Subscriber Portal managing the full lifecycle (upgrade, pause, resume, cancel, gift), and a Loyalty programme where tiers, streaks, XP and payment-anchored benefits turn one-off buyers into long-term members. It's a surface where a 1% conversion lift is measurable in weeks, a race condition costs real money, and complex financial state has to feel obvious at 2 a.m. on a phone, mid-queue.
We're looking for a Frontend Engineer who wants to be the person writing that code. You'll work in a modern stack - React 19, Next.js 16, TypeScript, TanStack Query, an in-house design system, Storybook + Chromatic + MSW - inside a monorepo of ~14 Subscription-owned packages. You'll ship alongside Product, Design and Backend, on features and experiments that move numbers the whole company watches.
**The Team**
You'll ship alongside a senior Frontend Engineer - your closest technical partner - plus two Backend Engineers, a Product Designer, a Product Manager and an Engineering Manager. Product and Design own the flows; you and the senior FE own how they land in production.
**What You'll Own**
* **The paid conversion path, end-to-end.** Conversion points across the app, the plan landing page, Stripe & Xsolla checkout (including gifting and upgrades), and the immediate post-purchase experience - you'll own the code, the experiments, and the conversion numbers they produce;
* **The subscriber lifecycle.** Pause, resume, cancel, renewal and the Subscriber Portal - where retention is won or lost. You'll build the flows that reduce voluntary churn without dark patterns and recover involuntary churn cleanly;
* **The Loyalty programme UI.** Tiers, streaks, XP, payment-anchored benefits, shop token allocation, badges. You'll turn our Loyalty service into an experience players actually understand, care about, and come back for;
* **Experimentation velocity.** Feature-flagged rollouts, A/B tests on pricing, bundling, activation and cancel-flow interventions, wired to analytics with the rigour to trust the results;
* **The technical health of a revenue-critical surface.** Testing culture (Vitest + Storybook + Chromatic + MSW), observability, and the safe-rollout discipline that lets us ship confidently to code that processes real transactions every minute.
**What We Are Looking For**
* Solid production experience with **React 19, TypeScript, and Next.js** (App Router);
* Fluent with modern data-layer patterns - **TanStack Query** (or equivalent) and **Redux Toolkit** - and a clear point of view on when to reach for each;
* Comfortable in a **large monorepo**: package boundaries, dependency hygiene, incremental migrations, working across many consumers of your code;
* Track record of **owning a high-traffic, business-critical surface** - checkout, billing, payments or another revenue/retention path - and understanding the operational demands (idempotency, error recovery, race conditions, safe rollout, observability, and the uptime discipline that treats every minute of downtime as lost revenue);
* **Strong eye for details** of complex state in production: proration, entitlements, expirations, currency and tax, localisation, accessibility. You know the common pitfalls and handle them in code, not in post-mortems;
* Familiarity with **experimentation tooling and mechanics**: feature flags, segmentation, A/B tracking, and the instrumentation that makes results trustworthy;
* Solid on **testing culture** - unit, component and visual regression. You don't ship revenue code without a safety net;
* **Collaborative by default**: fluent code review, clear writing, low-ego debates, comfortable partnering with Product, Design and Backend as equals;
* Fluent with **modern AI coding tools** (Copilot, Cursor, Claude Code or similar) as part of your daily practice - and clear-eyed about when to lean on them and when not to, especially on revenue-critical code.
**Bonus skills**
* Passionate about learning new, cutting-edge technologies and finding applicable business cases as needed;
* A passion for video games and esports is a plus.

# Analyst - Advanced Materials, Chemicals & Ingredients ("AMCI") (Industrials Team) - London
London, United Kingdom
## Job Description
Lazard is one of the world’s preeminent financial advisory and asset management firms. **Our people and culture make the difference**. While global in presence and reach, ours is a close, collaborativecommunity of just over 3,000 professionals. Lazard is a place of continuous knowledge sharing, skill development and relationship building, where professionals grow and succeed together. Our entrepreneurial culture, flat structure and embrace of individual differences, allow creative ideas, original concepts, and unique perspectives to drive our business forward — and for careers to take flight.
Through our financial advisory business, Lazard advises clients around the world on strategic and financial matters including mergers and acquisitions, restructurings, capital structure and capital raising. Our client relationships are built on trust and discretion. As the world’s largest advisory-focused firm, we have exceptional depth of expertise across industry sectors and geographies. We value the rich diversity that comes from blending local perspective with our global network. **Analyst – London**
We are looking for a proactive, enthusiastic and motivated individual, with at least 1.5 years M&A experience, to join the AMCI team in London.
The AMCI team in London works across a highly international client and project base, advising on transactions throughout continental Europe, China, MEA and North America. The team benefits from strong and consistent deal flow, offering hands‐on deal exposure across both buy‐ and sell‐side M&A. Our work spans a broad range of industries and end‐markets and is closely coordinated with Lazard colleagues across global offices, giving team members meaningful cross‐border collaboration and visibility, including travel as project needs arise. **Role and Responsibilities:**
Responsible for the day-to-day support of transaction and marketing efforts and conducting company and industry analysis on new transaction opportunities. **We’ll trust you to:**
* Demonstrate strong technical and analytical skills with an ability to build financial models with ease;
* Research, analyse, sensitise and adapt both internal and client-facing financial and statistical analysis/ models;
* Efficiently evaluate qualitative and quantitative data;
* Be responsible for assisting in the preparation and production of presentations and marketing materials for clients and prospective clients, in consultation with other team members;
* Effectively manage your own work, taking responsibility for accuracy and quality-checking finished products with regards to content, consistency and language;
* Assist senior bankers on an ad hoc basis as needed with various reports and analyses;
* Handle execution and process matters flawlessly, assisting in due diligence efforts as appropriate;
* Use your own knowledge and judgement to add information to presentations where appropriate;
* Communicate effectively and appropriately;
* Be a proactive team participant with a natural ability to develop their profile across Lazard groups and regions;
* Independently develop sound and logical views whilst understanding both the big picture and the minutiae;
* Show confidence, professionalism and accountability at all times;
* Contribute to firm-wide initiatives including recruiting, training and professional development.
**You’ll need to have:**
* Gained a minimum of 1.5 years of M&A experience within an investment banking environment *(no prior sector knowledge is necessary)*;
* Robust understanding of the accounting principles that underlie typical financial analyses used in advisory (particularly valuation);
* Outstanding financial understanding that can be readily translated into modelling that is used for both marketing and execution purposes;
* Self-motivation, with demonstrable ability to manage conflicting priorities and requests in a high pressure environment;
* The ability to take initiative and function independently, balanced with strong team skills;
* Excellent interpersonal and relationship-building skills, with the ability to maintain relationships with colleagues and clients at all levels;
* Strong verbal and written communication skills;
* The ability to deliver requested materials to senior bankers in a timely manner;
* Strong awareness of the regulatory environment;
* The skills to maintain high standards of professional and ethical conduct, adhere to legal and regulatory requirements of the banking environment and follow Lazard policies and procedures;
* Minimum 2.1 university degree classification (or equivalent if studied outside the UK);
**What we offer**
We strive to enhance the total health and well-being of our employees through comprehensive, competitive benefits. Our goal is to offer a highly individualised employee experience that enables you to balance your commitments to career, family, and community. When you work for Lazard, you are working for an organisation that cares about your unique talents and passions, and will continue to invest in the development of your career. **Does this sound like you?**
Apply! We’ll get in touch with the next steps. **Representation at Lazard**
Lazard is an intellectual capital business committed to delivering the best advice and solutions to clients. To achieve these objectives, we focus on attracting, developing and retaining the best talent. We believe that a workforce comprised of people who represent a wide array of backgrounds, experiences and perspectives creates a rich variety of thought that empowers us to challenge conventional wisdom, solve problems creatively and make better decisions.
Lazard was built on the premise that a multicultural firm can best serve a global clientele. As a global firm that has grown organically from local roots in different countries, we have a deep tradition of respecting and appreciating individual differences. Doing so has been core to our success for over 175 years. We are committed to sustaining an environment where every colleague is supported in their professional pursuits, can maximize their individual potential and contribute to our collective success. #LI-HB1

# Fund Accountant
The Fund Accounting team is based in our London office and works closely with other support functions across the business. As the number of funds continues to grow, we are looking for a motivated Fund Accountant who is keen to learn, develop and contribute to the team. The successful candidate will support daily P&L, NAV, valuations, reconciliations and reporting, and will bring strong analytical skills, attention to detail and the ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment
## Key Responsibilities
* Manage the daily P&L process, including the attribution of P&L by driver;
* Produce daily, weekly and monthly fund return estimates and attribution;
* Support the full month-end close process, including:
+ Adhering to the valuation source hierarchy and overall valuation policy;
+ Assisting the administrator in obtaining independent confirmation of external valuations; and
+ Reconciling estimated NAV and P&L to final NAV and P&L.
* Monitor daily valuation changes to ensure that movements are consistent with market drivers;
* Prepare monthly, quarterly and ad hoc reports for senior management, summarising P&L attribution, fund performance, key drivers, significant changes and any risks to business continuity;
* Assist with new business initiatives, fund launches, new products and new corporate structures;
* External reporting, including
+ Assist with the preparation of annual audited financial statements; and
+ Assist with the preparation and review of regulatory reporting, including Form PF and AIFMD reporting;
* Initiate and facilitate process improvements.
**General**
* Provide day-to-day support to colleagues within the team and across the wider organisation;
* Any other duties commensurate with the post holder’s position and seniority; and
* All employees should understand that it is their personal responsibility to comply with all organisational, statutory and regulatory policies and procedures.
## Skills, Knowledge and Expertise
* Relevant experience in fund accounting, product control or a related finance role, ideally within asset management or financial services
* Experience of NAV, P&L, reconciliations, valuations or financial reporting;
* Advanced Excel skills and proficiency in other Microsoft Office applications;
* A proactive approach to process improvement; VBA experience would be advantageous;
* Strong analytical skills and attention to detail;
* Strong written and verbal communication skills.
**Educational & Professional Qualifications**
* Educated to degree level or equivalent;
* Strong academic results in subjects relevant to the role; and
* Newly qualified, or close to completing a relevant professional qualification, such as ACA, ACCA, CIMA or equivalent.
## Benefits
Systematica Investments provides you with excellent benefits from day 1. We provide private medical insurance for you and your immediate family. We offer competitive salaries combined with an attractive bonus and pension plus free drinks and snacks at the office. We also offer paid parental leave with enhanced leave for mothers/primary carers.
We are an equal opportunity employer and value diversity at our company.

Tangem is a high-tech company in the blockchain sector was founded in 2017, headquartered in Zug, Switzerland, with branches in North America, Eastern Europe, and APAC.
Tangem started with the idea of bringing digital assets to the masses using a unique combination of a smartcard-based hardware wallet and mobile applications. Company owns and promotes the technology of hardware cold-wallet for digital assets with secure and simple UX in 220 countries today. Our customers enjoy setup time within 1 minute with the ultimate security level for digital assets on their wallet. Tangem solutions offer multi-support of a growing number of thousands of tokens by a single wallet. SBI Crypto Investment Ltd., the digital asset venture investment company wholly owned by SBI Holdings Inc., has invested $15 million into Tangem in 2019 for mass adoption of blockchain technology.
* Senior-level independence;
* Ability to ask questions and a desire to improve;
* Proficiency in Swift;
* Experience with async/await;
* Experience with SwiftUI, Combine - from 2 years;
* Knowledge of basic frameworks (UIKit, Foundation);
* Object-oriented programming (OOP) skills, understanding of SOLID principles;
* Familiarity with modern architectural patterns, principles of functional programming, protocol-oriented design;
* Understanding of Rest API and HTTP principles.
Nice to have:
* Published projects on the App Store;
* Experience with CryptoKit;
* Understanding of blockchain technology principles.
* Development of the main Tangem mobile application;
* Creation of public libraries (SDK) for integrating company products into third-party solutions;
* Active participation in technical discussions, design, and development of new features;
* Writing unit tests.
* Stability, development, participation in the future unicorn's growth;
* We use the latest technologies, no legacy, leveraging SwiftUI and Combine;
* Remote work from anywhere in the world, with a schedule aligned with GMT+3;
* Competitive salary in EUR/USDT;
* Unlimited vacation;
* Birthday presents;
* Compensation for the purchase of necessary technical devices for the work;
* Paid sick leave.

