## Corporate Actions Analyst
Apply
: London, United Kingdom
: Full time
: Posted Today
: R94804
# # **About Us**
**Wellington Management** offers comprehensive investment management capabilities that span nearly all segments of the global capital markets. Our investment solutions, tailored to the unique return and risk objectives of institutional clients in more than 60 countries, draw on a robust body of proprietary research and a collaborative culture that encourages independent thought and healthy debate. As a private partnership, we believe our ownership structure fosters a long-term view that aligns our perspectives with those of our clients.
# # About the Role
# Role Overview
The Corporate Actions team is a part of the Portfolio Operations Team within Investment Operations. Investment Operations provides each of Wellington’s investment teams with the data, controls, and support they need to ensure that their investment intent is accurately reflected in accordance with client regulatory and operational requirements. Other teams within Investment Operations include Derivative/Trade Operations, Portfolio Guideline Monitoring, Performance & Benchmark, Reference Data & Securities Valuation, and Portfolio Accounting.
The Corporate Actions Analyst is responsible for the day-to-day activities associated with managing and processing of all corporate events. The Analyst will work in a team setting and communicate regularly with other groups within Investment Operations, and across the firm globally, including Trading, Portfolio Management, Legal, Performance, Derivative Operations, Private Equity, and Global Relationship Management. They will also serve as a resource to junior members of the team for market and event knowledge, escalations, and guidance.
Primary Responsibilities
* Work closely with Wellington’s corporate action service providers, custodians, and internal clients to develop and improve sound workflows;
* Support Portfolio Management teams by providing analysis and understanding of complex voluntary events;
* Execute daily processing/validation procedures while ensuring the integrity and consistency of global corporate action data across multiple platforms, and in alignment with market practice;
* Research and resolve in-conflict action details, communicate voluntary instructions, and confirm client entitlements;
* Identify and implement process improvements and system enhancements that increase efficiencies and/or reduce risk for the team and/or the firm;
* Work with internal and external groups to resolve complex action issues; and
* Represent Corporate Actions at interdepartmental and external meetings.
Qualifications
The successful candidate for this position is likely to have:
* 5-7 years of relevant work experience with a focus on corporate actions and portfolio accounting;
* Highly knowledgeable of the life cycle of global corporate action events across all asset classes and products. Specific market and/or tax withholding knowledge a plus;
* Experience with derivatives, especially corporate action processing on derivatives is a plus;
* Experience reviewing Market/Company offering documents to interpret and communicate event details correctly and concisely to the firm;
* Experience working with vendor products and technology;
* Able to effectively operate in a fast-paced work environment while managing risk, deadlines, and ambiguities;
* Analytical in approach to issue resolution;
* Customer Service competency with excellent verbal and written communication skills; and
* Possess a passion for intellectual curiosity, problem solving, and continuous learning.
Location
The role will be based in Wellington’s London office, Cardinal Place, 80 Victoria Street, London, SW1E 5JL.
Not sure you meet 100% of our qualifications? That’s ok. If you believe that you could excel in this role, we encourage you to apply and welcome a chance to review your background. We are dedicated to building and maintaining a diversified workforce and considering a broad array of candidates with a variety of skill, workplace experiences, and backgrounds.
*As an equal opportunity employer, Wellington Management ensures that all qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment without regard to* *race, color, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, religion, creed, national origin, age, ancestry, disability (physical or mental), medical condition, citizenship, marital status, pregnancy, veteran or military status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by applicable law***.* If you are a candidate with a disability, or are assisting a candidate with a disability, and require an accommodation to apply for one of our jobs, please email us at GMWTalentOperations@wellington.com**.*
We believe that in person interactions inspire and energize our community and are essential to our culture. In support of this commitment, our employees work from our offices 4 days a week with flexibility to work remotely 1 day a week. We believe that this approach ultimately supports our mission to deliver investment excellence to our clients and their beneficiaries over the long term.

Reporting to our Data Protection Team Lead, the Data Protection Consultant will work directly with our clients to scope, analyse and implement GDPR practices, processes and procedures. In addition to this, the GDPR Consultant role will complete and oversee the delivery of gap analyses, implementations and DPO services to our wide variety of customers.
In this role, you will be providing support with the handling and processing of Data Subject Access Requests (DSARs). The role will involve assisting with reviewing information, carrying out redactions where required, and supporting the wider team throughout the DSAR process. Full training and guidance will be provided, making this a great opportunity for someone looking to develop their knowledge and experience in data protection and compliance.
Due to the nature of the role, the position requires the ability to manage multiple clients simultaneously whilst ensuring a customer-centric approach.
Responsibilities:
Lead and manage GDPR projects, ensuring delivery is in line with client expectations;
Act as an SME for all GDPR, PECR and other privacy-related matters;
Work closely with the Sales to scope projects;
Conduct GDPR Gap Analyses and GDPR Implementations (data mapping, developing policies and procedures, records of processing, DPIAs, LIAs etc.);
Work closely with the GDPR Team Lead to oversee the project management, scheduling and delivery of all GDPR projects, completing and updating relevant records for reporting purpose.
Deliver GDPR training as well as supporting clients with GDPR documentation, data breaches, and data subject access requests;
Write content for articles and blog posts on data protection related topics;
Any other appropriate job duties in line with the associated skill and experience of the post holder.
Skills and experience required:
Direct experience of leading Data Protection consultancy projects (scoping, gap analysis, and implementation) across small, medium and large businesses, with a strong understanding of tailored service delivery to suit client size and requirements;
Qualified in one or more of the following: GDPR Practitioner (or equivalent), Certified DPO, IAPP CIPP/E qualification, Law Degree with a focus on GDPR/Privacy;
Knowledge of CCPA and other international privacy laws highly desirable;
Specific region or sector expertise (e.g., Scotland, Northern Ireland, health and social care, financial services) highly desirable
Strong Microsoft Office skills;
Personal Attributes:
Ability to remain calm under pressure and meet deadlines; Strong organisational skills with a high attention to detail; Ability to prioritise and handle multiple tasks at any given time; Pro-active and enthusiastic with a can do attitude; Excellent verbal and written communication skills;
Strong commercial acumen; Ability to work on own initiative as well as being a team player;
Willingness to learn.
Other:
International and national travel should be expected as part of the role;
Must be eligible to live and work in the UK;
WorkNest Benefits:
Annual leave: 25 days, increasing by 1 day per each completed year of service up to a maximum of 28 days, plus statutory bank holidays which will be paid.
Birthday Day Off: One additional day off for your birthday, to be taken a week either side of your birthday
Private Medical Insurance Discounted individual coverage (available after successful completion of probation). Full individual cover after 3 years.
Subsidised Gym / Wellbeing membership £15 per month subsidised membership (available after probation)
VITO Days: 2 paid volunteer days per year (available after probation)
Health Cash Plan Cash back on dental, optical and more, Employee Assistance Programme, Virtual GP and wellbeing resources (available from day one)
UK Electric Vehicle Salary Sacrifice Scheme Subject to eligibility criteria
Enhanced Family Related Leave Pay subject to qualifying periods
Company Sick Pay 2 weeks enhanced sick pay (available after probation)
Pension Standard Life Salary Sacrifice Pension - 3% Employer / 5% Employee. Auto-enrolment after 3 months, with the option to opt in or opt out
Sophos Home Premium Cover for your family personal laptops
Employee referral scheme £1000 paid to you for successful employee referrals
Social events
If you’re looking for an opportunity to develop your career in data protection and work with a wide range of clients, we’d love to hear from you.
At WorkNest, you’ll be part of a supportive and collaborative team where you’ll have the opportunity to build your expertise, take on new challenges and make a real impact for our clients.
If this sounds like the right opportunity for you, we’d encourage you to apply and tell us why you’d be a great addition to the team.

# Contract Product Owner (Remote EU - UK timezone)
Remote
* **Location:**Remote (EU based, GMT timezone)
* **Department:** Product
* **Employment Type:** Contract
* **Contract Length:** 6 months (with potential for extension)
### About YLD:
Our goal is to help our clients keep moving forward. We work with them to build the skills and capabilities they need to stay ahead of the competition, and we know our success only happens when they succeed. We’re a team of curious, talented people, and we’re committed to making YLD a place where great people want to work, grow, and stay.
We’re a remote-first consultancy specialising in software engineering, product design, and data. Our teams are based across London, Lisbon, and Porto, and we create digital solutions that continue to deliver value long after our work is done.
### About the role:
As a Product Owner at YLD, you’ll be part of a client team building innovative products. We’re looking for someone curious, passionate, driven, and enthusiastic. You should be skilled in problem-solving and experienced in turning a product vision into a roadmap and a backlog a team can deliver against. You’re also an effective communicator and a strong team player. Together with your team, you’ll thrive in a fast-paced delivery environment, delivering outstanding results and exciting projects.
### Your day-to-day responsibilities:
**Product vision and management**
* Collaborate with the client on product vision, set your team goals and guide the team to ensure they meet the goals of the client’s wider objectives;
* Develop a deep understanding of customer personas, jobs-to-be-done and product behaviours;
* Lead a cross-functional team and identify customer needs to help the team deliver innovative solutions to satisfy those needs;
* Develop and prioritise a roadmap with the team and internal and external partners, along with a coherent product backlog that supports it.
**Backlog management**
* Collaborate with stakeholders to define and prioritise product features based on business goals, stakeholder expectations and market needs;
* Manage the backlog to ensure that it is up-to-date, relevant, and actionable for development teams;
* Work alongside the client on discovery for new features;
* Optimise the best technical solutions to avoid over- and under-engineering problems, making sure that the development effort focuses on the right areas, in collaboration with the tech lead;
* Track and monitor features’ performance and functionality after launch to ensure continuous improvement and iterations.
### Preferred qualifications:
* Proven experience as a Product Owner or Product Manager, taking digital products from discovery through to launch;
* Experience leading a cross-functional delivery team in an agile environment (Scrum, Kanban or similar);
* Confident writing and refining user stories and acceptance criteria, and running backlog refinement with a development team;
* Comfortable using prioritisation frameworks to make trade-offs and their rationale clear to stakeholders;
* Experience using analytics, experimentation and user research to inform product decisions;
* Experience working with senior stakeholders in a client-facing or consultancy setting;
### You should apply if you are:
* Self-motivated, proactive and always looking for ways to improve and develop yourself;
* A good communicator, both in writing and verbally. You’ll be able to explain technical ideas and concepts in business-friendly language;
* Detail oriented;
* Possess strong problem-solving skills that balance innovation with pragmatic technology choices to solve business needs;
* Used to working in a team-oriented, collaborative environment;
* Analytical and problem-solving-oriented;
* A genuine believer in diversity and fairness.
### **What you’ll get in return:**
* The chance to work with a forward-thinking, ethical, and fun group of people and to develop and grow your skills in a fast-moving business
### **Our typical recruitment process:**
* 1st Interview with a Talent Partner (30/45 mins)
* Technical Interview with our Head of Design (1h30)
* Final meet & greet with the project's Client Partner (1h30)
